%% §21 machine 4 of 8 — Campaign Order  (Prisma enum: OrderState)
%% §21: DRAFT -> SENT -> ACCEPTED / REJECTED -> ACTIVE -> COMPLETED / CANCELLED
%% One of the two machines §38 names explicitly. The commercial record, per athlete.
    direction TB
    [*] --> DRAFT : terms drafted from the accepted invite
    DRAFT --> SENT : sent to the athlete
    SENT --> ACCEPTED : athlete accepts the terms
    SENT --> REJECTED : athlete rejects the terms
    SENT --> CANCELLED : withdrawn before response (derived)
    ACCEPTED --> ACTIVE : work may begin
    ACTIVE --> COMPLETED : all deliverables VERIFIED
    ACTIVE --> CANCELLED : campaign or order cancelled
    COMPLETED --> [*]
    REJECTED --> [*]
    CANCELLED --> [*]

    note right of ACCEPTED
      Acceptance writes an AgreementAcceptance row
      carrying a hash of the exact text shown.
      Compensation and usage rights are snapshotted
      onto the order — later rate changes do not
      alter a signed order.
    end note
    note right of COMPLETED
      COMPLETED is what makes the athlete's Earning
      ELIGIBLE. See machine 7.
    end note
